-- title:
--   Kronecker's congruence for j(q) and j(qᵖ)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime (nonzero as a natural number). Write $F_p = \mathbb{Q}(\,\{\,\mathrm{qExpand}_{\mathbb Q,d}(j_q) : d \mid p,\ d \neq 0\,\}\,)$ for the intermediate field `modularFunctionFieldFull p` of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the substitutions $q \mapsto q^{d}$ applied to the Laurent series $j_q = q^{-1}\cdot(\text{the rational-coefficient power series } j\mathrm{Num})$, the substitution $\mathrm{qExpand}_{\mathbb Q,d}$ being the ring endomorphism of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ obtained by multiplying exponents by $d$; inside $F_p$, let $j =$ `IgusaScheme.jFull p` be the element given by $j_q$ itself. Let $jp \in F_p$ be an element whose underlying Laurent series is $\mathrm{qExpand}_{\mathbb Q,p}(j_q)$, i.e. $j(q^p)$. The assertion is that there exists $w$ in the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra $\mathbb{Z}[j, jp]$ of $F_p$ generated by the two-element set $\{j, jp\}$ such that $$(j^{p} - jp)\,(j - jp^{\,p}) = p\cdot w$$ holds in $F_p$, the factor $p$ being the image of the natural number $p$ under the canonical map into $F_p$.
--
--   This is Kronecker's congruence $\Phi_p(X,Y) \equiv (X^p - Y)(X - Y^p) \pmod p$ for the modular polynomial, in the shape of a relation between the elements $j(q)$ and $j(q^p)$ of the level-$p$ modular function field, with the congruence witnessed by an explicit element of $\mathbb{Z}[j(q), j(q^p)]$. It feeds [`ModularCurve.DRModel.jFull_sub_pow_mem_nonunits_of_valuationSubring_pair`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModel.jFull_sub_pow_mem_nonunits_of_valuationSubring_pair), where the product of the two factors being divisible by $p$ forces one of them into the maximal ideal of a valuation subring.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_sub_mul_sub_eq_natCast_mul_of_coe_eq_qExpand.lean

